 "text": "Hey! How are you feeling? Of course. The key things are rice, pasta and bread, most veg, most fruit, most berries, most nuts and seeds. Read the labels. Looking for gluten free or no gluten is a start, but some flours are genuinely safe, like quinoa flour or rice flour. Then look at the label. It often says gluten free or has a yellow sticker. Soy sauce is usually fine, but check the label. I' glad. Let me know if you think of anything else. That's a common reaction. It' a big adjustment, but she'll find her favorite foods again.",
